module tecs.assets

--[[
Acquires assets without blocking the host, and owns what a caller holds.

A load returns the asset. There is no future, no promise and no callback in the
game-facing signature: a request that cannot answer at once parks its coroutine
through `nupp.suspension` and resumes with the answer, so the same call reads the
same way inside a frame system and inside a startup script.

```nupp
local assets <const> = require("tecs.assets")

local loader = app.assets
local handle, reason = loader:request(assets.bytes, "levels/one.json")
if handle == nil then
    return nil, reason
end
local text <const> = handle:value() as string
handle:release()
```

[`Application`](tecs.application.Application) creates `app.assets` and shuts it
down after world shutdown. Standalone tools may use `newAssets` and must call
`shutdown` themselves. Settled handles remain valid until their owners release
them; stopping the loader cancels acquisitions, not those existing holds.

Inside a system the same two lines suspend the logical update rather than the
thread, and the host renders the frames that pass while the file is read. Where
no suspension handler is installed, the built-in driver runs the readiness pumps
on this thread and the call still returns the asset.

## What this module owns, and what it does not

This is orchestration: requesting, sharing an acquisition between callers that
want the same thing, counting holds, replacing a payload in place and reporting
a failure to the call that asked for it. Reading bytes, decoding pixels,
uploading a texture and freeing a native allocation belong to a
[`Kind`](tecs.assets.Kind), which supplies a
[`Job`](tecs.assets.Job) per acquisition and a `release` for the payload
it produced. A GPU service registers a kind whose job issues its own upload
command; nothing about textures is written here.

## Failure

An invalid argument raises at the call: an empty path, a released handle, a
loader that has shut down. A load that could not produce its asset answers
`nil, reason` from `request`, whether it failed before parking or hours later.
The readiness pump never raises a load failure of its own, because the call that
asked for the asset is the only place the reason means anything; the pump
resumes that call and lets it return the pair its signature promises.

## Holds and residency

A [`Handle`](tecs.assets.Handle) is a hold, not a cache entry. Two
requests for one path that overlap share one acquisition and receive holds on
one handle, because decoding the same file twice at once duplicates work without
producing another result. A request made after the first settles acquires again:
nothing here retains a settled asset behind the caller's back, and the payload
lives exactly as long as the holds on it.

`release` gives up one hold, and the last one frees the payload through the
kind. Releasing a handle already down to nothing does nothing, so a shutdown
path need not know whether something else got there first.

## Replacement

`reload` acquires the same path again and swaps the result into a handle every
holder already has, then frees what it displaced. The handle's identity does not
change and its `revision` advances, which is what a consumer holding device
state keyed on the handle watches to know its copy is stale. A failed reload
leaves the resident payload exactly as it was and answers `false, reason`.
]]

local files = require("nupp.io.files")
local suspension = require("nupp.suspension")
local log = require("nupp.log")

--- Where one acquisition stands.
export type Status = "pending" | "ready" | "failed"

--- One acquisition in progress, owned by the kind that opened it.
---
--- A job is driven by the loader's readiness pump, never by the caller. It runs
--- on whatever the kind uses underneath: a file read, a worker channel, a native
--- service reply. Nothing here assumes which.
export record Job
    --- Advances the acquisition and reports where it stands.
    ---
    --- Answers `"pending"` alone while the work continues, `"ready"` and the
    --- payload once it is done, or `"failed"` and a non-empty reason. The loader
    --- stops calling it after the first answer that is not `"pending"`, and the
    --- payload it hands back becomes the loader's to free through the kind.
    poll: function(): (Status, any?, string?)

    --- Abandons the acquisition and frees anything it holds.
    ---
    --- The loader calls it at most once, and only for a job that has not
    --- answered `"ready"` or `"failed"`. It must not raise.
    cancel: function(): nil
end

--- How one class of asset is acquired and freed.
---
--- A payload is whatever the kind's job produced, so this layer types it as
--- `any` and the caller casts once at `value`. A phantom type parameter would
--- move that cast rather than check it, and the loader would still be handing
--- back what the job supplied.
export record Kind
    --- Read-only. Contains the content kind name this asset is recorded under,
    --- which is the string file watching and tooling filter on.
    name: string

    --- Read-only. Begins one acquisition of `path`.
    ---
    --- Answers the job that will produce the payload, or `nil, reason` where the
    --- acquisition cannot start at all. A refusal here reaches the requesting
    --- call without parking it.
    open: function(path: string): (Job?, string?)

    --- Read-only. Frees one payload after its last hold goes. Nil where the
    --- collector owns the payload outright, which is true of a plain Lua string.
    release: (function(value: any): nil)?
end

-- Compatibility surface. Content kind names are what a file-watching filter and
-- the debug tools name, so they keep the spelling the SDL implementation
-- recorded through `content.note` even though the loader around them is new.

--- Read-only. Names the content kind of a file loaded without interpretation.
export const DOCUMENT = "document"

--- Read-only. Names the content kind of a decoded image.
export const IMAGE = "image"

--- Read-only. Names the content kind of a loaded sound.
export const SOUND = "sound"

--- Read-only. Names the content kind of a loaded font.
export const FONT = "font"

--- Read-only. Names the content kind of a loaded shader.
export const SHADER = "shader"

--- Read-only. Names the content kind of a decoded model scene.
export const MODEL = "model"

--- A caller's hold on one acquired asset.
---
--- Handles are shared: every caller whose request joined one acquisition gets
--- this same object, and the payload lives until the last of them releases it.
export record Handle
    --- Read-only. Contains the requested path unchanged. The loader does not
    --- resolve it, so it is whatever the caller passed.
    path: string

    --- Read-only. Contains the content kind name this asset was acquired under.
    kind: string

    --- Engine-owned. Counts the callers holding this payload. Ordinary game code
    --- reads `holds` instead.
    private refs: integer

    --- Engine-owned. Holds the acquired payload until the last release, and nil
    --- after it. Ordinary game code reads `value` instead.
    private payload: any?

    --- Engine-owned. Counts the replacements this handle has taken. Ordinary
    --- game code reads `revision` instead.
    private replacements: integer

    --- Engine-owned. Frees the payload at the last release, or nil where the
    --- collector owns it.
    private free: (function(value: any): nil)?

    --- Engine-owned. Names the loader that counts this handle as resident.
    private owner: Assets

    value: function(borrows self: Handle): any?
    resident: function(borrows self: Handle): boolean
    revision: function(borrows self: Handle): integer
    holds: function(borrows self: Handle): integer
    retain: function(exclusive self: Handle): nil
    release: function(exclusive self: Handle): nil
end

--- One caller waiting on one acquisition.
local record Waiter
    live: boolean
    claimed: boolean
    resume: (function(boolean): nil)?
end

--- One acquisition, and the callers waiting on it.
local record Entry
    owner: Assets
    key: string
    path: string
    kindName: string
    job: Job
    free: (function(value: any): nil)?
    status: Status
    payload: any?
    reason: string?
    handle: Handle?
    waiters: {Waiter}
end

--- A loader: the acquisitions in flight, the holds they produced, and the
--- readiness pump that advances them.
---
--- One loader per application. Two loaders share nothing, which is what makes a
--- test able to shut one down without disturbing anything else in the process.
export record Assets
    --- Engine-owned. Indexes acquisitions in flight by kind and path so two
    --- overlapping requests share one. Ordinary game code reads `pending`.
    private entries: {[string]: Entry}

    --- Engine-owned. Holds the same acquisitions in a stable order the readiness
    --- pump walks without allocating.
    private order: {Entry}

    --- Engine-owned. Counts acquisitions in flight.
    private inFlight: integer

    --- Engine-owned. Counts handles still holding a payload.
    private residentCount: integer

    --- Engine-owned. Numbers private replacement acquisitions so two reloads
    --- never share an entry.
    private serial: integer

    --- Engine-owned. Holds the callers parked in `drain`.
    private drainers: {Waiter}

    --- Engine-owned. Holds the registered readiness pump until shutdown.
    private pump: suspension.Source?

    --- Engine-owned. Reports whether this loader still accepts requests.
    private open: boolean

    request: function(exclusive self: Assets, kind: Kind, path: string): (Handle?, string?)
    reload: function(exclusive self: Assets, kind: Kind, handle: Handle): (boolean, string?)
    drain: function(exclusive self: Assets): (boolean, string?)
    pending: function(borrows self: Assets): integer
    resident: function(borrows self: Assets): integer
    running: function(borrows self: Assets): boolean
    shutdown: function(exclusive self: Assets): nil
end

local logger = log.named("tecs.assets")

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Jobs supplied by this module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- Begins a complete file read that settles on the readiness pump.
---
--- The read itself runs in the pump's pass rather than in the requesting call,
--- so a request for a file parks and resumes exactly as one for a decoded asset
--- does. A kind that needs the bytes before it can do its own work composes this
--- job rather than reading the file inline.
---
--- @param path the file to read
--- @return the job that answers the complete bytes
--- @return a failure reason, when the read cannot be started
export function readJob(path: string): (Job?, string?)
    if path == "" then
        return nil, "a file read needs a path"
    end
    local finished = false

    return new Job(
        poll = function(): (Status, any?, string?)
            if finished then
                return "pending"
            end
            finished = true
            local bytes, reason = files.read(path)
            if bytes == nil then
                return "failed", nil, reason or ("cannot read " .. path)
            end

            return "ready", bytes
        end,
        cancel = function(): nil
            finished = true
        end
    )
end

--- Reads a complete file into a binary-safe string without interpreting it.
---
--- A handle of this kind carries a `string`, so `handle:value() as string` is
--- the cast its caller writes. The collector owns the string and the kind frees
--- nothing. Releasing the handle still matters: it is what tells the loader the
--- asset is no longer resident.
export const bytes: Kind = new Kind(name = DOCUMENT, open = readJob, release = nil)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entries
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local function freePayload(entry: Entry): nil
    local payload = entry.payload
    entry.payload = nil
    if payload == nil then
        return
    end
    local free = entry.free
    if free ~= nil then
        free(payload)
    end
end

--- Counts the waiters that have not abandoned this acquisition.
local function liveWaiters(entry: Entry): integer
    local count: integer = 0
    local waiters = entry.waiters
    for index = 1, #waiters do
        if waiters[index].live then
            count = count + 1
        end
    end

    return count
end

local function wake(waiter: Waiter): nil
    local resume = waiter.resume
    if resume == nil then
        return
    end
    waiter.resume = nil
    resume(true)
end

--- Detaches a settled or abandoned acquisition from the loader.
local function forget(self: Assets, entry: Entry): nil
    if self.entries[entry.key] ~= entry then
        return
    end
    self.entries[entry.key] = nil
    local order = self.order
    for index = #order, 1, -1 do
        if order[index] == entry then
            order[index] = order[#order]
            order[#order] = nil
            break
        end
    end
    self.inFlight = self.inFlight - 1
end

--- Records one acquisition's outcome and wakes everyone waiting on it.
---
--- A ready payload becomes one handle holding one reference per live waiter. An
--- acquisition every waiter abandoned is freed here rather than leaked to a
--- handle nobody will release.
local function settle(self: Assets, entry: Entry, status: Status, payload: any?, reason: string?): nil
    entry.status = status
    entry.payload = payload
    entry.reason = reason
    if status == "ready" then
        local holders = liveWaiters(entry)
        if holders == 0 then
            freePayload(entry)
        else
            local handle = new Handle(
                path = entry.path,
                kind = entry.kindName,
                refs = holders,
                payload = payload,
                replacements = 0,
                free = entry.free,
                owner = self
            )
            entry.handle = handle
            entry.payload = nil
            self.residentCount = self.residentCount + 1
        end
    else
        logger:debug("%s load failed: %s: %s", entry.kindName, entry.path, reason or "failed")
    end
    local waiters = entry.waiters
    for index = 1, #waiters do
        wake(waiters[index])
    end
end

--- Hands one settled acquisition to one waiter.
local function claim(entry: Entry, waiter: Waiter): (Handle?, string?)
    waiter.claimed = true
    waiter.live = false
    if entry.status == "ready" then
        local handle = entry.handle
        if handle == nil then
            return nil, "the asset was released before this caller took it"
        end

        return handle
    elseif entry.status == "failed" then
        return nil, entry.reason or "the asset could not be loaded"
    else
        return nil, "the acquisition did not settle"
    end
end

--- Gives up one waiter's place in an acquisition without taking its result.
---
--- Reached when a park is abandoned: the host stopped, a task scope was
--- cancelled, or the surrounding suspension extent ended. A waiter that had
--- already been given a hold gives it back, because the call that would have
--- taken it is unwinding instead of returning.
local function abandon(self: Assets, entry: Entry, waiter: Waiter): nil
    if waiter.claimed or not waiter.live then
        return
    end
    waiter.live = false
    waiter.resume = nil
    local handle = entry.handle
    if handle ~= nil then
        handle:release()

        return
    end
    if entry.status ~= "pending" or liveWaiters(entry) > 0 then
        return
    end
    forget(self, entry)
    entry.job.cancel()
end

--- Advances every acquisition in flight and settles the ones that answered.
local function drive(self: Assets): integer
    if self.inFlight == 0 then
        return 0
    end
    local settled: integer = 0
    local order = self.order
    for index = #order, 1, -1 do
        local entry = order[index]
        if entry.status == "pending" then
            local status, payload, reason = entry.job.poll()
            if status ~= "pending" then
                forget(self, entry)
                settle(self, entry, status, payload, reason)
                settled = settled + 1
            end
        end
    end
    if self.inFlight == 0 and #self.drainers > 0 then
        local waiting = self.drainers
        self.drainers = {}
        for index = 1, #waiting do
            wake(waiting[index])
        end
    end

    return settled
end

--- Registers `waiter` on `entry` and parks until the acquisition settles.
---
--- The value the park carries is only a wake signal. The outcome lives on the
--- entry, so a caller resumed by the pump reads the same settled acquisition a
--- caller that never parked reads.
---
--- The loader reaches this through `entry.owner` rather than through a
--- parameter, because the cancellation this answers with outlives the call and
--- may therefore capture nothing the caller only lent it.
local function park(entry: Entry, waiter: Waiter, pump: suspension.Source?, operation: string): nil
    suspension.suspend(operation, function(resume: function(boolean), context: suspension.Context): (function()?)
        if waiter.claimed or not waiter.live or entry.status ~= "pending" then
            resume(true)

            return nil
        end
        waiter.resume = resume
        if pump ~= nil then
            context:uses(pump)
        end

        return function(): nil
            abandon(entry.owner, entry, waiter)
        end
    end)
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The loader
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- Creates a loader with nothing in flight and its readiness pump registered.
---
--- The pump reports itself inactive while nothing is in flight, so a program
--- with no suspension handler never sleeps on a loader that has no work.
---
--- @return the running loader
export function newAssets(): Assets
    local loader = new Assets(
        entries = {},
        order = {},
        inFlight = 0,
        residentCount = 0,
        serial = 0,
        drainers = {},
        pump = nil,
        open = true
    )
    loader.pump = suspension.source(
        "tecs.assets",
        10,
        function(): integer
            return drive(loader)
        end,
        nil,
        function(_: suspension.Source): boolean
            return loader.inFlight > 0
        end
    )

    return loader
end

--- Requests one asset and returns the caller's hold on it.
---
--- The call suspends only while the acquisition is pending. Two overlapping
--- requests for one kind and path share the acquisition and receive holds on one
--- handle; a request made after the first settles acquires again.
---
--- @param self the running loader
--- @param kind how this class of asset is acquired and freed
--- @param path the asset path, passed to the kind unchanged
--- @return the caller's hold, which it releases when its consumer has taken
---   ownership
--- @return a failure reason, when the asset could not be acquired
--- @raises when the path is empty or the loader has shut down
function Assets.request(exclusive self: Assets, kind: Kind, path: string): (Handle?, string?)
    if not self.open then
        error("assets.request: the loader has shut down", 2)
    end
    if path == "" then
        error("assets.request: path must not be empty", 2)
    end
    local key = kind.name .. "\0" .. path
    local entry = self.entries[key]
    if entry == nil then
        local job, reason = kind.open(path)
        if job == nil then
            return nil, reason or ("cannot load " .. path)
        end
        entry = new Entry(
            owner = self,
            key = key,
            path = path,
            kindName = kind.name,
            job = job,
            free = kind.release,
            status = "pending",
            payload = nil,
            reason = nil,
            handle = nil,
            waiters = {}
        )
        self.entries[key] = entry
        self.order[#self.order + 1] = entry
        self.inFlight = self.inFlight + 1
    end
    local waiter = new Waiter(live = true, claimed = false, resume = nil)
    entry.waiters[#entry.waiters + 1] = waiter
    if entry.status == "pending" then
        park(entry, waiter, self.pump, "tecs.assets.request")
    end

    return claim(entry, waiter)
end

--- Acquires an asset again and replaces what a handle already holds.
---
--- Every holder sees the new payload through the handle it already has, and the
--- handle's `revision` advances so a consumer keyed on it can tell its own copy
--- is stale. The displaced payload is freed through the kind once the swap has
--- happened. A failed acquisition changes nothing and reports why.
---
--- @param self the running loader
--- @param kind how this class of asset is acquired and freed
--- @param handle the resident handle to replace in place
--- @return whether the handle now holds a newly acquired payload
--- @return a failure reason, when the acquisition failed
--- @raises when the loader has shut down, the handle is released, or the handle
---   belongs to another loader or another kind
function Assets.reload(exclusive self: Assets, kind: Kind, handle: Handle): (boolean, string?)
    if not self.open then
        error("assets.reload: the loader has shut down", 2)
    end
    if handle.owner ~= self then
        error("assets.reload: the handle belongs to another loader", 2)
    end
    if handle.kind ~= kind.name then
        error("assets.reload: the handle was acquired as " .. handle.kind, 2)
    end
    if handle.refs <= 0 then
        error("assets.reload: the handle has been released", 2)
    end
    local job, reason = kind.open(handle.path)
    if job == nil then
        return false, reason or ("cannot load " .. handle.path)
    end
    -- A replacement never shares an acquisition: it ends in a swap into one
    -- named handle rather than in a handle of its own, and two callers cannot
    -- both perform that swap on one payload.
    self.serial = self.serial + 1
    local entry = new Entry(
        owner = self,
        key = kind.name .. "\0" .. handle.path .. "\0replace\0" .. tostring(self.serial),
        path = handle.path,
        kindName = kind.name,
        job = job,
        free = kind.release,
        status = "pending",
        payload = nil,
        reason = nil,
        handle = nil,
        waiters = {}
    )
    self.entries[entry.key] = entry
    self.order[#self.order + 1] = entry
    self.inFlight = self.inFlight + 1
    local waiter = new Waiter(live = true, claimed = false, resume = nil)
    entry.waiters[#entry.waiters + 1] = waiter
    if entry.status == "pending" then
        park(entry, waiter, self.pump, "tecs.assets.reload")
    end
    local replacement, failure = claim(entry, waiter)
    if replacement == nil then
        return false, failure or "the asset could not be reloaded"
    end
    local acquired = replacement.payload
    replacement.payload = nil
    replacement.refs = 0
    self.residentCount = self.residentCount - 1
    if handle.refs <= 0 then
        -- Every hold went while the replacement was in flight, so there is
        -- nothing left to swap into and the new payload is freed instead of
        -- being written into a handle nobody will release.
        local free = kind.release
        if free ~= nil and acquired ~= nil then
            free(acquired)
        end

        return false, "the handle was released while the replacement was loading"
    end
    local displaced = handle.payload
    handle.payload = acquired
    handle.replacements = handle.replacements + 1
    if displaced ~= nil then
        local free = handle.free
        if free ~= nil then
            free(displaced)
        end
    end

    return true
end

--- Suspends until nothing is in flight.
---
--- This is the startup and shutdown barrier, and it waits on every acquisition
--- this loader owns rather than only the caller's. It returns at once when
--- nothing is pending.
---
--- @param self the running loader
--- @return whether the loader drained
--- @return a failure reason, when the loader shut down while draining
--- @raises when the loader has already shut down
function Assets.drain(exclusive self: Assets): (boolean, string?)
    if not self.open then
        error("assets.drain: the loader has shut down", 2)
    end
    while self.inFlight > 0 do
        local waiter = new Waiter(live = true, claimed = false, resume = nil)
        self.drainers[#self.drainers + 1] = waiter
        local pump = self.pump
        -- The loop condition above already read the count, and nothing runs
        -- between there and here, so the subscription re-reads nothing and
        -- captures only values it owns.
        suspension.suspend("tecs.assets.drain", function(
            resume: function(boolean),
            context: suspension.Context
        ): (function()?)
            waiter.resume = resume
            if pump ~= nil then
                context:uses(pump)
            end

            return function(): nil
                waiter.live = false
                waiter.resume = nil
            end
        end)
        if not self.open then
            return false, "the loader shut down while draining"
        end
    end

    return true
end

--- Returns the number of acquisitions still in flight.
---
--- @param self the loader to inspect
--- @return every acquisition this loader owns, including replacements, and not
---   only one caller's
function Assets.pending(borrows self: Assets): integer
    return self.inFlight
end

--- Returns the number of handles still holding a payload.
---
--- @param self the loader to inspect
--- @return the count of handles with at least one hold left
function Assets.resident(borrows self: Assets): integer
    return self.residentCount
end

--- Reports whether this loader still accepts requests.
---
--- @param self the loader to inspect
--- @return false once `shutdown` has run
function Assets.running(borrows self: Assets): boolean
    return self.open
end

--- Stops the loader and reports the stop to every parked caller.
---
--- Every acquisition in flight is cancelled and every parked request resumes and
--- returns `nil, reason` from the call that asked for the asset, rather than
--- raising somewhere the reason means nothing. Handles that already settled keep
--- their payloads and still release correctly, so this frees nothing a caller
--- still holds.
---
--- Calling it twice does nothing the second time.
---
--- @param self the loader to stop
function Assets.shutdown(exclusive self: Assets): nil
    if not self.open then
        return
    end
    self.open = false
    local pump = self.pump
    if pump ~= nil then
        self.pump = nil
        pump:release()
    end
    local order = self.order
    self.order = {}
    self.entries = {}
    self.inFlight = 0
    for index = 1, #order do
        local entry = order[index]
        if entry.status == "pending" then
            entry.status = "failed"
            entry.reason = "the loader shut down while the asset was loading"
            entry.job.cancel()
            local waiters = entry.waiters
            for position = 1, #waiters do
                wake(waiters[position])
            end
        end
    end
    local waiting = self.drainers
    self.drainers = {}
    for index = 1, #waiting do
        wake(waiting[index])
    end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Handles
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- Returns the payload this handle holds.
---
--- The kind that acquired it decides what this is, so the caller casts once:
--- `handle:value() as Image`. Nothing below checks that cast.
---
--- @param self the handle to read
--- @return the payload, or nil once the last hold has gone
function Handle.value(borrows self: Handle): any?
    return self.payload
end

--- Reports whether the payload is still in memory.
---
--- @param self the handle to test
--- @return whether at least one hold remains
function Handle.resident(borrows self: Handle): boolean
    return self.refs > 0
end

--- Returns how many times this handle's payload has been replaced.
---
--- A consumer that keeps device state derived from the payload stores the
--- revision beside it and re-derives when the two differ.
---
--- @param self the handle to read
--- @return zero for a handle that has never been reloaded
function Handle.revision(borrows self: Handle): integer
    return self.replacements
end

--- Returns the number of callers holding this payload.
---
--- @param self the handle to read
--- @return the remaining hold count, which is zero once the payload is freed
function Handle.holds(borrows self: Handle): integer
    return self.refs
end

--- Takes one more hold on this payload.
---
--- Call it when passing a handle somewhere with a lifetime of its own, so the
--- two owners release independently.
---
--- @param self the handle to hold
--- @raises when the payload has already been freed
function Handle.retain(exclusive self: Handle): nil
    if self.refs <= 0 then
        error("assets.retain: the handle has been released", 2)
    end
    self.refs = self.refs + 1
end

--- Gives up this caller's hold, and frees the payload at the last one.
---
--- Call it once whatever needed the asset has taken ownership. Releasing a
--- handle already down to nothing does nothing, so a shutdown path need not know
--- whether something else got there first.
---
--- @param self the handle to release
function Handle.release(exclusive self: Handle): nil
    if self.refs <= 0 then
        return
    end
    self.refs = self.refs - 1
    if self.refs > 0 then
        return
    end
    local payload = self.payload
    self.payload = nil
    self.owner.residentCount = self.owner.residentCount - 1
    if payload == nil then
        return
    end
    local free = self.free
    if free ~= nil then
        free(payload)
    end
end
